{
  "an3.64:0.1": "Numbered Discourses 3.64 ",
  "an3.64:0.2": "7. The Great Chapter ",
  "an3.64:0.3": "With Sarabha ",
  "an3.64:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "an3.64:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Rājagaha, on the Vulture’s Peak Mountain. ",
  "an3.64:1.3": "Now at that time a wanderer named Sarabha had recently left this teaching and training. ",
  "an3.64:1.4": "He was telling a crowd in Rājagaha, ",
  "an3.64:1.5": "“I learned the teaching of the ascetics who follow the Sakyan, ",
  "an3.64:1.6": "then I left their teaching and training.” ",
  "an3.64:1.7": "Then several mendicants robed up in the morning and, taking their bowls and robes, entered Rājagaha for alms. ",
  "an3.64:1.8": "They heard what Sarabha was saying. ",
  "an3.64:1.9": "",
  "an3.64:1.10": "",
  "an3.64:2.1": "Then, after the meal, when they returned from almsround, they went up to the Buddha, bowed, sat down to one side, and said to him, ",
  "an3.64:2.2": "“The wanderer named Sarabha has recently left this teaching and training. ",
  "an3.64:2.3": "He was telling a crowd in Rājagaha: ",
  "an3.64:2.4": "‘I learned the teaching of the ascetics who follow the Sakyan, ",
  "an3.64:2.5": "then I left their teaching and training.’ ",
  "an3.64:2.6": "Worthy sir, please go to the wanderers’ monastery on the bank of the Serpentine River to see Sarabha the wanderer out of sympathy.” ",
  "an3.64:2.7": "The Buddha consented with silence. ",
  "an3.64:3.1": "Then in the late afternoon, the Buddha came out of